# TODO
## Authentication & authorization

- [X] Authenticate submitters: invite → session token (`bbr_user_…`, SHA-256 in `user_sessions.token_hash`); only they can POST /user/messages
- [ ] Moderator/admin role: only they can approve, reject, list messages and see sender_ip (still a single static `ADMIN_TOKEN`)
- [X] Per-printer API tokens: SHA-256 hash in `printers.token_hash`, plain token returned once on create, `RequirePrinterToken` middleware puts the printer ID in the request context
- [X] Printer routes take the printer ID from the token instead of the URL (`/printer/heartbeat`, `/printer/messages/oldest/claim`)
- [X] Token rotation endpoint: `POST /admin/printers/{id}/rotate_token`
- [X] Printers can only update their own messages: processed/printed/failed scoped by `printer_id`; another printer's message returns 404, like an unknown ID
- [ ] Token revocation without issuing a new one (set `token_hash` to NULL, e.g. when retiring a printer)
- [X] Group routes in chi behind role-specific middleware (`/admin`, `/printer`, `/user`)
- [X] Decide which printers a submitter may target: `user_printers`, managed with `PUT /admin/users/{id}/printers`
- [X] Take sender_name from the logged-in identity, so people can't impersonate others (`sender_id` → `users.name`)
- [X] Admin routes for users: create with invite, reissue invite, list/revoke sessions
- [ ] Write `user_sessions.last_used_at`: it exists in the schema and in the sessions response but is never set, so it is always `null`. Update it in `RequireUserToken` (or in `GetUserIDBySessionHash`), throttled to avoid a write on every request, e.g. `UPDATE user_sessions SET last_used_at = NOW() WHERE id = $1 AND (last_used_at IS NULL OR last_used_at < NOW() - INTERVAL '5 minutes')`. Useful to spot and revoke stale devices. Otherwise drop the column.
- [ ] Persistent session cookie (see `SCRATCHPAD.md`): `POST /users/claim` sets `__Host-bbr_session` (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, Max-Age 400 days) instead of returning the token in the body; `RequireUserToken` reads the bearer header, then the cookie; clear the cookie on 401; refresh it together with the throttled `last_used_at` update

## Approval flow

- [X] SubmitMessage: set initial status (pending / awaiting_approval) based on source instead of always pending
- [X] CreateMessage: Validate PrinterID
- [X] SubmitAdminMessage
